{{Short description|None}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The final round of the [[1950 FIFA World Cup]] took place from 9 to 16 July 1950. The final round consisted of [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Spain national football team|Spain]], [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]], and [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140614002515/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2013/m=12/news=brazil-first-world-cup-draw-2238709.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=14 June 2014 |title=Brazil's first World Cup draw |date=3 December 2013 |publisher=FIFA}}</ref> The winners of the final round were declared winners of the World Cup.

Uruguay won the tournament, defeating hosts Brazil in the [[Uruguay v Brazil (1950 FIFA World Cup)|decisive match]] for their second World Cup title.<ref>{{cite news| url=http://sportsillustrated.cnn.com/2010/soccer/world-cup-2010/writers/jonathan_wilson/07/04/uruguay.history/index.html | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100707110332/http://sportsillustrated.cnn.com/2010/soccer/world-cup-2010/writers/jonathan_wilson/07/04/uruguay.history/index.html | url-status=dead | archive-date=7 July 2010 | work=CNN | title=Uruguay's 1950 World Cup triumph a testament to the spirit of garra | date=4 July 2010}}</ref>

